  'train.b4.l1':'Guided 20-minute routine','train.b4.l2':'Sleep and fatigue tracking in the app','train.b4.l3':'Deload week every 5 weeks',

  'food.eyebrow':'Nutrition','food.title':'The feasting table',
  'food.lede':'Our coaching starts from the Nordic dietary pattern, one of the best-studied in Europe, and tunes it for a body that trains hard. You eat a lot, you eat well, and you are never hungry.',
  'food.c1.t':'Protein on every plate','food.c1.d':'Between 1.6 and 2.2 g per kilo of body weight daily, spread across 3–5 meals. Fatty fish, eggs, fermented dairy, lean meat and legumes. This is what protects your lean mass when you push.',
  'food.c2.t':'Northern whole grain','food.c2.d':'Oats, rye and barley as your energy base. High satiety, fermentable fibre and sustained release: you reach training with fuel and without crashes.',
  'food.c3.t':'Roots, brassicas and berries','food.c3.d':'Beetroot, carrot, turnip, cabbage, kale and forest berries. Enormous food volume for very few calories — the trick to genuine fullness without overshooting.',
  'food.c4.t':'Fat that earns its place','food.c4.d':'Rapeseed oil, nuts and oily fish two or three times a week. Omega-3, vitamin D and satiety without reaching for ultra-processed food.',
  'food.c5.t':'No starvation diets','food.c5.d':'No savage deficits. We set calories in sustainable ranges and build around high-satiety foods, because a plan you abandon is worth nothing.',
  'food.c6.t':'Adapted to your land','food.c6.d':'Whether you live in Helsinki, Oslo, London or Madrid, your plan uses what your supermarket actually stocks. Same principles, different basket.',

  'sci.eyebrow':'The evidence','sci.title':'Why it works (and where it is published)',
  'sci.lede':'We invent nothing. We gather existing evidence on high-velocity training and the Nordic dietary pattern, and apply it with judgement.',
  'sci.1.t':'Speed protects bone','sci.1.d':'In postmenopausal women, power training maintained bone mineral density over two years, while traditional progressive resistance training did not achieve the same.',
  'sci.2.t':'High velocity in older adults','sci.2.d':'A systematic review of high-velocity resistance training examines its effects on bone mineral density in older adults — a setting where the fast stimulus is especially relevant.',
  'sci.3.t':'Power, balance and daily life','sci.3.d':'Comparing slow versus fast execution, both increase strength, but only high-velocity training improves muscle power production, with greater gains in balance, mobility and confidence.',
  'sci.4.t':'Explosive exercise and bone remodelling','sci.4.d':'A 10-week programme combining jogging with explosive power exercises produced significant increases in femoral neck and shaft bone density, with the jump squat among the most effective stimuli.',
  'sci.5.t':'Nordic pattern and cardiometabolic health','sci.5.d':'A systematic review and meta-analysis published in Diabetologia found small but consistent reductions in non-HDL cholesterol, apolipoprotein B, fasting insulin, body weight, BMI and systolic blood pressure.',
  'sci.6.t':'Oats and barley: gut and inflammation','sci.6.d':'A systematic review of randomised controlled trials describes how oats and barley shift gut microbiota composition, with anti-inflammatory effects in metabolically at-risk populations.',
  'sci.disclaimer':'Notice: Viking Fitness is a training and nutrition education service, not medical treatment. The cited evidence supports the principles of the method; it does not promise individual results. If you have a medical condition, are pregnant or take medication, consult your doctor before starting.',

  'app.eyebrow':'Your saga, recorded','app.title':'The clan app',
  'app.lede':'Everything you do gets written down. Sessions, sets, loads, meals, calories, macros, weight and measurements. The app computes your weekly volume, your trend and your rank within the clan.',
  'app.l1':'Training log with sets, reps and kilos',
  'app.l2':'Food diary with calories and macros, including a Nordic food database',
  'app.l3':'Body weight tracking with a trend chart',
  'app.l4':'Consistency streak and rank progression: from Thrall to Einherjar',
  'app.l5':'Your data stays in your browser — nothing leaves your device',
